==Central Franconian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|gmw-cfr|ein||Kölsch; Westerwald}}
* {{alt|gmw-cfr|ään||eastern Moselle Franconian}}

===Etymology===
{{dercat|gmw-cfr|gmw-pro|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=3}}
From {{inh|gmw-cfr|gmh|een}}, from {{inh|gmw-cfr|goh|ein}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gmw-cfr|/eːn/}}

===Numeral===
{{head|gmw-cfr|numeral}}

# {{lb|gmw-cfr|Ripuarian|western|_|Moselle Franconian}} [[one]]
#: {{ux|gmw-cfr|Loß mich der nur '''een''' Frooch stelle.|Let me ask you just '''one''' question.}}
#: {{ux|gmw-cfr|Wanns de keene Steff häs, kann ich der '''eener''' jevve.|If you don't have a pencil, I can give you '''one'''.}}

====Declension====
* Nominative/Accusative:
** Attributive: {{m|gmw-cfr|[[ee]] Mann}} or {{m|gmw-cfr|[[eene]] Mann}}, {{m|gmw-cfr|[[een]] Frau}}, {{m|gmw-cfr||ee Kend}}. The form {{m|gmw-cfr||ee}} becomes {{m|gmw-cfr||een}} before vowels and optionally elsewhere, whereas the feminine is always {{m|gmw-cfr||een}}.
** Independent without determiner: {{m|gmw-cfr|eener}} or {{m|gmw-cfr||eene|g=m}}, {{m|gmw-cfr||een|g=f}}, {{m|gmw-cfr|eent}} or (younger) {{m|gmw-cfr|eens|g=n}}.
** Independent with determiner: {{m|gmw-cfr||dä/die/dat een}} or {{m|gmw-cfr||dä/die/dat eene}}.
* Dative:
** Without determiner: {{m|gmw-cfr||eenem Mann}}, {{m|gmw-cfr||eener Frau}}, {{m|gmw-cfr||eenem Kend}}.
** With determiner: {{m|gmw-cfr||däm eene|g=m}}/{{g|n}}, {{m|gmw-cfr||dä eene}} or {{m|gmw-cfr||dä eener|g=f}}.
* Eastern Moselle Franconian distinguishes masculine nominative and accusative. Masculine {{m|gmw-cfr||ää, ääner}} are nominative, whereas masculine {{m|gmw-cfr||ääne}} is accusative.
* Westernmost Ripuarian has no dative forms. Moreover it uses the velarised stem {{m|gmw-cfr||eng-}} before vocalic endings and always in the feminine.

